# Store text files with LF line endings in git, and let each computer use its
# own line endings when checking files out (CRLF on Windows, LF on Mac/Linux).
* text=auto

# The dataset must stay byte-for-byte identical on every computer: the pipeline
# identifies documents by a hash of their exact bytes, and CFTC_2022.txt and the
# CSV files use Windows (CRLF) line endings. So git must never convert them.
data/** -text

# Binary files, never converted.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary